{
  "title": "Mallet Toe",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7015/mallet-toe",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 7 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mallet Toe is a lesser toe deformity characterized by hyperflexion of the DIP joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with DIP joint hyperflexion with neutral PIP and MTP joints in a lesser toe.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a trial of nonoperative management with shoe modification and toe sleeves. Surgical management is indicated for progressive deformity, fixed contractures, and dorsal toe ulcerations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "contracture (or spasm) of FDL because of pressure of toe against the end of shoe",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "> 70% of patients have a longer digit",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "rupture of EDL at DIP joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Deformity may be",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "flexible or fixed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Congenital mallet toe",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with **flexion and lateral deviation** of the DIP joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
